    {
      "image": "videos/03-ai-designed-cure/2.jpg",
      "seconds": 25.65,
      "text": "The patient had an infection that beat every antibiotic. So doctors turned to phages, viruses that hunt bacteria and ignore human cells entirely. Medicine has used them for a century. The problem is finding one that fits your particular infection. That search can take months. This time, in October 2026, an AI lab designed the phage instead. Days, not months.",
