    {
      "image": "videos/03-ai-designed-cure/3.jpg",
      "seconds": 25.63,
      "text": "Antibiotics are a hammer. They flatten everything in reach, which is why bacteria keep learning to duck. A phage is a key, cut to one lock. For a hundred years we could only find keys already lying on the ground. Now we can cut them. And the same hands that cut a key can, in principle, cut a crowbar. Which is exactly the conversation this field is now forced to have.",
